<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:32Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump promises Americans $5,000 if Republicans win midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79b266576e610c27b919df887f782e8b194e05a36c91723ec732205fc6321c4f</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T03:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-promises-americans-5-000-if-republicans-win-midterms/a-79208399--193518c15bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-promises-americans-5-000-if-republicans-win-midterms/a-79208399?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president gave a wide-ranging speech at the Republican midterm convention. He defended the war in Iran, trade wars and tariffs, and the White House ballroom. He also called Democrats evil and immigrants animals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: Several killed, dozens missing after fire on ferry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a72899593a49df1a97e62ee7d24cf24d16d48b0104838b4a10501086c14b4d0d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T01:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-several-killed-dozens-missing-after-fire-on-ferry/a-79208236--4b1ef54015f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-several-killed-dozens-missing-after-fire-on-ferry/a-79208236?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Footage released by the Coast Guard showed the vessel engulfed in flames as rescuers brought bodies ashore in body bags. The ship's manifest listed 134 passengers and crew.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Finland: Google announces €13 billion AI, energy investment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4713db96984ef40ee0eafccafe831122257f6b715ee1ecd0465c3bb4d8802044</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T22:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-google-announces-_13-billion-ai-energy-investment/a-79208034--066f4655241f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-google-announces-€13-billion-ai-energy-investment/a-79208034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Google has announced a plan to expand AI data centers and buy massive amounts of nuclear energy. Finland's security services have warned of there are risks, but the right-wing government says the deal will bring jobs.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's PM: Zelenskyy's plane almost hit by drone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c1135e0d0a6cadc0f699a432b879f3e520440b0525e65225c9d6cdf4afb162d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T20:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-pm-zelenskyy-s-plane-almost-hit-by-drone/a-79207528--c78d6300cd95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-pm-zelenskyy-s-plane-almost-hit-by-drone/a-79207528?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone nearly struck a plane carrying Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy from Moldova to Oslo, according to Norway's prime minister. However, a Ukrainian source said the threat may have been overstated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China: English to be removed as a graded core subject?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:508aaebce0ba0b75b316f72d9394ad060b1740861ed94fdeed0f11373c7dc199</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629--52f7a1cb9d3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A university professor is calling for English to no longer be taught as a graded core subject in Chinese schools. Opponents argue that, in a globalized world, knowing English is beneficial for the country and career.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ceuta: Documents show Spanish intelligence warned of crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f256316f3472150e2cbdadd127845e24962fa12f4a70737305bfeb3fd833dd9</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ceuta-documents-show-spanish-intelligence-warned-of-crisis/a-79206505--1dd65a7f978d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ceuta-documents-show-spanish-intelligence-warned-of-crisis/a-79206505?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain declassified documents that showed warnings issued a day before more than 70,000 migrants rushed the Ceuta border fence. Meanwhile, the EU announced funds to strengthen the border and return migrants to Morocco.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11, 2001 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:906dced0787da2a940588a14eb9fcf77743e955b056e97359a763defb3bf4902</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918--22a07e00351f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg, via the so-called Hamburg cell, whose members played key roles in the plot. A look back at a day that shook up Germany’s approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e658c79a180d1f124012533e7d8cbd09668bfbe19fb3257f41ad2cc0dea54ae</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Switzerland: Two killed in power plant explosion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:336e598cb7fc37c48d685d1bc0697d43d91d6955c20db08e08e633766aa4dcdb</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/switzerland-two-killed-in-power-plant-explosion/a-79205516--3f73e13d5b04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/switzerland-two-killed-in-power-plant-explosion/a-79205516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fire and subsequent explosion have killed two workers at a Swiss hydroelectric power plant. Authorities say the facility suffered major damage in the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran tightens social control with crackdown on cafes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7bb1b2d391a9f564441785990bcd16cddc62f98965f83ce94e00667be198171</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988--56f8af8e2572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities are keeping a close eye on cafes, fearing they could play a role in fostering anti-government sentiment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's constitutional reform: What does it mean — especially for Abiy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b525a7d7a72116c6cb9ff072363dc6dc7d9735dc97ab3d0121818e0c6a36086</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262--7aa1de37183a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Does Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed stand to benefit from a planned constitutional reform in the country? A new presidential system would reshape political power — and could give him even more power in office.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Oil prices rise as Middle East conflict escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16af4d630f22d16ffb8411efd84bb673c9d291bc7f527e14bb000eb5455d9e01</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T14:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oil-prices-rise-as-middle-east-conflict-escalates/a-79203547--69f3e58c677b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oil-prices-rise-as-middle-east-conflict-escalates/a-79203547?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The price of oil returned to triple digits in US dollars, as conflict in the Middle East threatens supply chains and puts a strain on global reserves.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Syria arms depot explosion kills at least 14</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2690309a801d6ff1bdc39ef073e2ef86eb28b89e63ddcdf1e49e01c0739b62c6</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314--22d7b8669d08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion struck near the Syrian city of Sarmada in Idlib province in the northwest. The Defense Ministry said the weapons and remnants from the war were being stored temporarily at the site before being relocated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6e0c973e45c2afd8b9b36e42f8e51dcebfd1f66ef5f5421e7b25cc67a40a9ff</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters From the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why we're still looking for dark matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:459d46454443e1b478a5788463e4c71f3cad7b105af147c85930251bbc02119d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395--3bfbe0fa2ce3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When physicists said they may have spotted evidence of dark matter almost 100 years after it was proposed as a theory, the internet lit up. Here's why we're searching for the thing that holds everything else together.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49587ae4dbc78cfdc15d0968c8d08ad9e75fd94e5414ba57a6b3d3aa1a5bced7</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes more restrictions for Airbnb, holiday rentals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bec79878793ea3e7a9bd0a2623226a170f32baf1dfff93a680ac3e81e9f13d87</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-more-restrictions-for-airbnb-holiday-rentals/a-79202023--ad637f480100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-more-restrictions-for-airbnb-holiday-rentals/a-79202023?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants tighter rules on short-term rentals to tackle housing shortages in tourist hotspots.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: How  the 'house of sisters' threat split society</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bedb9c01b8fa0445e336327b93d793bf9d7a65b8218db2efffe0d03966402170</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163--b9de2b546f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rumor has it that the 'house of sisters' is where kidnapped women from other Syrian sects are forced to convert to Islam. Nobody knows if it really exists, but it's being used to create communal tensions anyway.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>LIV Golf in financial turmoil: what's next for the sport?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b5b8e10e4e80a556aac1c28d71bc005c6565cf300a6ffa56f3ea6ff2fb648eb</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569--378367d5fd0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald V laid to rest in state funeral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87f2501b2c00113b2e600051b6977eeeb79ba549ccce541a8bf8f1d80395682d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-v-laid-to-rest-in-state-funeral/a-79199812--18dfde6e8405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-v-laid-to-rest-in-state-funeral/a-79199812?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heads of state from around the world came to Oslo to pay tribute to the late monarch.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia dissolves parliament as snap elections called</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:344221875c6d6340f0d0f6126037304af3f6e9efa4b77874377bf98ddd5af8fc</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-dissolves-parliament-as-snap-elections-called/a-79200868--9098381ff4d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-dissolves-parliament-as-snap-elections-called/a-79200868?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serbia will head to the polls in late October after President Aleksandar Vucic dissolved parliament following growing pressure from protesters demanding political change. However, Vucic plans to stand as a PM candidate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
